                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e599c457-e6b2-3de1-9232-1022a8a8d323",
                        "entry_id": "f5b45ec3-8835-3c2f-9e5a-c0be94ceec9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An element of a lineage, especially of a lineage given in the Bible"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "nonstandard"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbf3872f-f704-4a5a-bd08-463eb7d39841",
                                "sense_id": "e599c457-e6b2-3de1-9232-1022a8a8d323",
                                "text": "To put food on the table, Ruth gleaned in the fields and one of the fields belonged to Boaz who noticed her and admired her. They married and Ruth bore a son, Obed. There ensues a begat-ridden genealogy and...."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c19aaa6c-5abb-42da-9417-2d4db8f7b887",
                                "sense_id": "e599c457-e6b2-3de1-9232-1022a8a8d323",
                                "text": "There's a bunch of begats in First Chronicles, chapter six, and it's way dull, especially if you consider what a begat involves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70c9db4a-653e-4784-b5bf-1887eadc57ad",
                                "sense_id": "e599c457-e6b2-3de1-9232-1022a8a8d323",
                                "text": "In many instances even that cannot be done,\" and John Edgar Wideman prefaces Damballah with \"A Begat Chart\" and a \"Family Tree.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "f36fbc8a-3ef0-34b3-a73b-90e53a7b2e39",
                "word": "begat",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8072230f-46a7-3721-a186-df53feea4f29",
                        "entry_id": "f36fbc8a-3ef0-34b3-a73b-90e53a7b2e39",
                        "glosses": [
                            "simple past of beget"
